set_note(address=CODE:0x0..0x1, note=Note(content=r#"VT520 firmware 23-010ED-00: a 512KB ROM holding eight 64KB banks. This database maps all of them into one 19-bit CODE space: bank N sits at CODE:0xN0000. P1.4, P1.5 and P1.6 select the bank (bit 4 is the low bit), and the whole 64KB space switches.
Cross-bank calls use trampoline slots: bit ops that change the bank, LCALL, bit ops that restore it, RET. A slot whose LCALL targets itself is an outgoing stub (bN_far_<target>). After the bank changes, the CPU fetches the LCALL at the same offset in the new bank, which is that bank's landing slot (bN_land_<target>) and calls the real routine. Some calls take two hops (bank 7 -> bank 3 -> bank 0).
Stub and landing names give the final target: a known name, or bN_XXXX for bank N address XXXX.
0x0000-0x0985 is nearly the same in every bank (vectors, ISRs, ROM test, trampolines). The CPU starts in bank 0, which jumps to 0x0982; SETB P1.6 there switches to bank 4, which forwards through its stub at 0x0E72 to bank 7's reset_entry."#, fields={}, id="00000000000000000000000000", links=[], tags=["banking"]))
